    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00001",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00288:title:sect-00001-title",
        "text": "Biological Aldol Reactions"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00001",
          "segmentId": "m00288:para:para-00001"
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00002",
          "segmentId": "m00288:para:para-00002"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00001",
          "class": "unnumbered",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00288:alt:fig-00001-alt",
              "text": "The scheme shows type one and two aldolase reactions. In both, dihydroxyacetone phosphate reacts with glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate yielding fructose 1,6-bisphosphate. Iminium ion is formed in type one on hydrolysis yields product."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_23_13_001.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00003",
          "segmentId": "m00288:para:para-00003"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00002",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00288:title:sect-00002-title",
        "text": "Biological Claisen Condensations"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00004",
          "segmentId": "m00288:para:para-00004"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00002",
          "class": "unnumbered",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00288:alt:fig-00002-alt",
              "text": "Malonyl A C P reacts with acetyl synthase generating enolate ion expelling carbon dioxide. The reaction expels synthase - S H, giving acetoacetyl A C P."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_23_13_002.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00005",
          "segmentId": "m00288:para:para-00005"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00003",
          "class": "unnumbered",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00288:alt:fig-00003-alt",
              "text": "The butyryl synthase and malonyl A C P reaction form 3-ketohexanoyl A C P. The product has six-carbon chain with two carbonyl groups positioned on the first and third carbon."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_23_13_003.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00003",
      "class": "chemistry-matters",
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00288:title:sect-00003-title",
        "text": "A Prologue to Metabolism"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00006",
          "segmentId": "m00288:para:para-00006"
        },
        {
